{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FYqvEiMg2gDKsuSpTdGRBg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Brief: check-in widget\n2\t\n3\ttype: feature\n4\tid: cup\n5\tbranch: feature/cup_check-in-widget\n6\tdate: 2026-10-29\n7\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\n8\t\n9\t## What\n10\t\n11\tA third home-screen widget: **today's check-in**. One row per enabled tracker\n12\t(mood, sleep, water, sports, …), each with its tappable values. Tapping a\n13\tvalue saves it for today; tapping the selected value again clears it, as in\n14\tthe app. At local midnight the widget resets to the new day. Tapping a\n15\ttracker's name opens the check-in page.\n16\t\n17\tIt builds on the multi-kind foundation and the action plumbing from the Your\n18\tDay and time tracking widgets. It adds one action type, `scale`. The API and\n19\tapp jobs live in other repos; their full contract is in this entry.\n20\t\n21\t**Prerequisite, done by a human before this job starts:** `frontend/` is\n22\tvendored from `solyto/app` with the job \"check-in widget: refresh on changes,\n23\troute key\". Confirm that `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` handles\n24\t`check_in`; do not run `scripts/vendor.sh`. If it is missing, stop and ask.\n25\t\n26\t## Why\n27\t\n28\tChecking in daily is quicker from the home screen than opening the app.\n29\t\n30\t## Contract with the API and the app\n31\t\n32\t### `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/check-in`\n33\t\n34\tSame headers, envelope and status codes as the other widgets. `data`:\n35\t\n36\t```\n37\t{\n38\t  \"kind\": \"check-in\", \"schema_version\": 1, \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n39\t  \"refresh_at\": \"<ISO 8601 with offset>\",       // next local midnight\n40\t  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },\n41\t  \"sections\": [{ \"key\": \"today\", \"rows\": [{     // one row per enabled tracker, at most 12\n42\t      \"id\": \"<tracker key>\",                      // e.g. \"mood\", \"food_quality\" (contains \"_\")\n43\t      \"title\": \"<translated tracker name>\",\n44\t      \"all_day\": true,\n45\t      \"route\": { \"key\": \"check_in\" },\n46\t      \"action\": {\n47\t        \"type\": \"scale\", \"key\": \"check_in.set\",\n48\t        \"value\": 3,                               // today's value, or null\n49\t        \"options\": [{ \"value\": 1, \"icon\": \"mood_1\", \"color\": \"#EF4444\" }, …]  // 5 or 6\n50\t      }\n51\t  }] }]\n52\t}\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\t- **Option icons:** `mood_1` … `mood_5` (Lucide angry, frown, meh, smile,\n56\t  laugh); `sport_dumbbell`, `sport_bike`, `sport_mountain`,\n57\t  `sport_footprints`, `sport_waves_ladder`, `sport_yoga`; and one icon per\n58\t  other tracker: `sleep`, `dreams`, `food_quality`, `food_amount`, `water`,\n59\t  `work`, `menstruation`, `alcohol`, `smoking`, `social_life`. Use the same\n60\t  icons as the app (`frontend/src/lib/components/check-in/daily/DailyCheckInIcon.svelte`)\n61\t  as vector drawables. An option with an unknown icon is not shown.\n62\t- **Colors** come from the server per option (`#RRGGBB`): tint the icon with\n63\t  it. Native has no color logic of its own.\n64\t- **No section title**: the widget title is enough.\n65\t- The section is left out when no tracker is enabled: show `labels.empty`.\n66\t- New in the format, backwards compatible: action type `scale` with `value`\n67\t  and `options`; Your Day and time tracking ignore it.\n68\t\n69\t### Action: `POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/check_in.set/<tracker key>`\n70\t\n71\tSame headers as the other actions **plus** `Content-Type: application/json`\n72\tand a body: `{ \"value\": <option value> }` to set, `{ \"value\": null }` to clear.\n73\tNative decides which: tapping the currently selected value sends `null`,\n74\tany other option sends its value. Always send the explicit target, never a\n75\t\"toggle\", so a retry cannot flip it.\n76\t\n77\t| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n78\t|---|---|---|\n79\t| 200 | Saved (also when the value was already set) | Re-fetch all placed widgets |\n80\t| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired | Delete the local token, show the signed-out state |\n81\t| 404 | Unknown tracker (or old server) | Re-fetch |\n82\t| 422 | Invalid value (should not happen from widget data) | Revert, short error state |\n83\t| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Revert, \"Please update the app\" |\n84\t| 429 / 5xx / no response | Rate-limited, server or network problem | Revert, short error state |\n85\t\n86\t### Route key\n87\t\n88\t`check_in` (no id): the app opens today's check-in.\n89\t\n90\t## Steps\n91\t\n92\t1. **Kind:** register `check-in` (path `/api/v1/widgets/check-in`, section\n93\t   key `today`) in the kind registry.\n94\t2. **Row ids:** widen the row id check (`WidgetPayload` `ROW_ID`) to allow\n95\t   `_`, so tracker keys like `food_quality` are valid. Keep the length limit.\n96\t3. **Parser:** read `scale` actions (`value`, `options` with `value`, `icon`,\n97\t   `color`); skip options with unknown icons or invalid colors; drop the\n98\t   action when no valid option is left.\n99\t4. **Actions with a value:** the action fill-in intent carries the tapped\n100\t   option's value; the receiver checks it is one of that row's options in the\n101\t   cached payload, computes the target (`null` when it equals the current\n102\t   `value`), and `WidgetApi.postAction` sends it as the JSON body. Actions\n103\t   without a value keep posting no body. Treat 422 like other failures.\n104\t5. **Widget** (`CheckInWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`, list via\n105\t   `RemoteCollectionItems`):\n106\t   - header with `labels.title` and \"updated at\", tapping it opens the app;\n107\t   - rows: the tracker name (tap → `navigate` with the row's `route`) and up\n108\t     to 6 option buttons, each an icon tinted with its color; the selected\n109\t     option gets a highlight background, as in the app;\n110\t   - while a row's action runs, that row is dimmed and ignores taps; on\n111\t     failure it reverts and shows the short error state;\n112\t   - set every view state explicitly (list rows are recycled);\n113\t   - the same states as the other widgets; light and dark; resizable;\n114\t     `appwidget-provider` XML with preview and description; a default size\n115\t     of about 4×3 (the list scrolls when more trackers are enabled).\n116\t6. **Strings** in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`: picker name and\n117\t   description, content descriptions for the option buttons (for example\n118\t   \"Mood: 3 of 5\"). Content text comes from the server. New strings go to the\n119\t   translator.\n120\t7. **Manual checks:** set mood, change it, tap it again (clears); pick a\n121\t   sport; check in in the app (the widget follows); change enabled trackers\n122\t   in the app (rows follow); after local midnight (or with the device clock\n123\t   moved) the widget shows an empty day; airplane mode while tapping (revert +\n124\t   error); logout; API 24 and 34+; light and dark; next to the other two\n125\t   widgets.\n126\t\n127\t## Out of scope\n128\t\n129\t- Other days than today; changing settings from the widget.\n130\t- Choosing trackers per widget (that would need the first widget setup\n131\t  screen).\n132\t- Fill-level icons (the app draws water, food amount and menstruation as\n133\t  filling icons; the widget uses one icon colored by value).\n134\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06ad74aa-1ba4-4cae-8c42-95d32284c601","uuid":"7d6404d9-2af2-4041-a001-9fe71b36e6a2","timestamp":"2026-10-29T20:51:51.926Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cup_check-in-widget/brief.md","content":"# Brief: check-in widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: cup\nbranch: feature/cup_check-in-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nA third home-screen widget: **today's check-in**. One row per enabled tracker\n(mood, sleep, water, sports, …), each with its tappable values. Tapping a\nvalue saves it for today; tapping the selected value again clears it, as in\nthe app. At local midnight the widget resets to the new day. Tapping a\ntracker's name opens the check-in page.\n\nIt builds on the multi-kind foundation and the action plumbing from the Your\nDay and time tracking widgets. It adds one action type, `scale`. The API and\napp jobs live in other repos; their full contract is in this entry.\n\n**Prerequisite, done by a human before this job starts:** `frontend/` is\nvendored from `solyto/app` with the job \"check-in widget: refresh on changes,\nroute key\". Confirm that `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` handles\n`check_in`; do not run `scripts/vendor.sh`. If it is missing, stop and ask.\n\n## Why\n\nChecking in daily is quicker from the home screen than opening the app.\n\n## Contract with the API and the app\n\n### `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/check-in`\n\nSame headers, envelope and status codes as the other widgets. `data`:\n\n```\n{\n  \"kind\": \"check-in\", \"schema_version\": 1, \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n  \"refresh_at\": \"<ISO 8601 with offset>\",       // next local midnight\n  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },\n  \"sections\": [{ \"key\": \"today\", \"rows\": [{     // one row per enabled tracker, at most 12\n      \"id\": \"<tracker key>\",                      // e.g. \"mood\", \"food_quality\" (contains \"_\")\n      \"title\": \"<translated tracker name>\",\n      \"all_day\": true,\n      \"route\": { \"key\": \"check_in\" },\n      \"action\": {\n        \"type\": \"scale\", \"key\": \"check_in.set\",\n        \"value\": 3,                               // today's value, or null\n        \"options\": [{ \"value\": 1, \"icon\": \"mood_1\", \"color\": \"#EF4444\" }, …]  // 5 or 6\n      }\n  }] }]\n}\n```\n\n- **Option icons:** `mood_1` … `mood_5` (Lucide angry, frown, meh, smile,\n  laugh); `sport_dumbbell`, `sport_bike`, `sport_mountain`,\n  `sport_footprints`, `sport_waves_ladder`, `sport_yoga`; and one icon per\n  other tracker: `sleep`, `dreams`, `food_quality`, `food_amount`, `water`,\n  `work`, `menstruation`, `alcohol`, `smoking`, `social_life`. Use the same\n  icons as the app (`frontend/src/lib/components/check-in/daily/DailyCheckInIcon.svelte`)\n  as vector drawables. An option with an unknown icon is not shown.\n- **Colors** come from the server per option (`#RRGGBB`): tint the icon with\n  it. Native has no color logic of its own.\n- **No section title**: the widget title is enough.\n- The section is left out when no tracker is enabled: show `labels.empty`.\n- New in the format, backwards compatible: action type `scale` with `value`\n  and `options`; Your Day and time tracking ignore it.\n\n### Action: `POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/check_in.set/<tracker key>`\n\nSame headers as the other actions **plus** `Content-Type: application/json`\nand a body: `{ \"value\": <option value> }` to set, `{ \"value\": null }` to clear.\nNative decides which: tapping the currently selected value sends `null`,\nany other option sends its value. Always send the explicit target, never a\n\"toggle\", so a retry cannot flip it.\n\n| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | Saved (also when the value was already set) | Re-fetch all placed widgets |\n| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired | Delete the local token, show the signed-out state |\n| 404 | Unknown tracker (or old server) | Re-fetch |\n| 422 | Invalid value (should not happen from widget data) | Revert, short error state |\n| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Revert, \"Please update the app\" |\n| 429 / 5xx / no response | Rate-limited, server or network problem | Revert, short error state |\n\n### Route key\n\n`check_in` (no id): the app opens today's check-in.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Kind:** register `check-in` (path `/api/v1/widgets/check-in`, section\n   key `today`) in the kind registry.\n2. **Row ids:** widen the row id check (`WidgetPayload` `ROW_ID`) to allow\n   `_`, so tracker keys like `food_quality` are valid. Keep the length limit.\n3. **Parser:** read `scale` actions (`value`, `options` with `value`, `icon`,\n   `color`); skip options with unknown icons or invalid colors; drop the\n   action when no valid option is left.\n4. **Actions with a value:** the action fill-in intent carries the tapped\n   option's value; the receiver checks it is one of that row's options in the\n   cached payload, computes the target (`null` when it equals the current\n   `value`), and `WidgetApi.postAction` sends it as the JSON body. Actions\n   without a value keep posting no body. Treat 422 like other failures.\n5. **Widget** (`CheckInWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`, list via\n   `RemoteCollectionItems`):\n   - header with `labels.title` and \"updated at\", tapping it opens the app;\n   - rows: the tracker name (tap → `navigate` with the row's `route`) and up\n     to 6 option buttons, each an icon tinted with its color; the selected\n     option gets a highlight background, as in the app;\n   - while a row's action runs, that row is dimmed and ignores taps; on\n     failure it reverts and shows the short error state;\n   - set every view state explicitly (list rows are recycled);\n   - the same states as the other widgets; light and dark; resizable;\n     `appwidget-provider` XML with preview and description; a default size\n     of about 4×3 (the list scrolls when more trackers are enabled).\n6. **Strings** in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`: picker name and\n   description, content descriptions for the option buttons (for example\n   \"Mood: 3 of 5\"). Content text comes from the server. New strings go to the\n   translator.\n7. **Manual checks:** set mood, change it, tap it again (clears); pick a\n   sport; check in in the app (the widget follows); change enabled trackers\n   in the app (rows follow); after local midnight (or with the device clock\n   moved) the widget shows an empty day; airplane mode while tapping (revert +\n   error); logout; API 24 and 34+; light and dark; next to the other two\n   widgets.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Other days than today; changing settings from the widget.\n- Choosing trackers per widget (that would need the first widget setup\n  screen).\n- Fill-level icons (the app draws water, food amount and menstruation as\n  filling icons; the widget uses one icon colored by value).\n","numLines":134,"startLine":1,"totalLines":134}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FYqvEiMg2gDKsuSpTdGRBg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
