{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXCRHZpFJDMzuWWeziGg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the check-in widget code (tasks 1–9), but it has never been compiled or run. This session had no JDK, Android SDK or emulator, so I couldn't run `./gradlew assembleDebug` or any of the manual checks in task 10.\n\n**What it does:**\n- **Rows:** the widget shows one row per enabled tracker, with up to 6 icon buttons tinted with the server's colors. The selected one is highlighted.\n- **Tapping an option:** it saves that value. Tapping the already-selected option clears it by sending an explicit `{\"value\": null}`. A tapped value is only accepted if it matches one of that row's options in the cached data.\n- **Tapping the tracker name:** it opens the check-in page.\n- **While a tap is being saved:** that row is dimmed and ignores taps. On failure it reverts and shows the short error line, as the other widgets do.\n- **Other widgets:** Your Day and time tracking still post their actions with no body, as before. Taps queued by an older app version also still go out without a body.\n\n**The 21 icons** were converted from Lucide (the same version the app uses) and the app's own custom icons. For the three trackers the app draws as filling icons, I used a single shape:\n- **Water:** a cup outline.\n- **Food amount:** a pizza slice.\n- **Menstruation:** a droplet outline.\n\n**Decisions you may want to check:**\n- **Error text:** I reused the existing \"Couldn't update\" string. The other existing error string reads \"checking off failed\" in German, which doesn't fit here.\n- **Fourth string:** I added `widget_check_in_option_selected` (\"Mood: 3 of 5, selected\") on top of the three planned, so screen readers announce which option is chosen. The \"3 of 5\" is the option's position in the row, not its raw value.\n- **Translations:** I wrote the German, French, Spanish and Italian strings myself, so the translator should still review them.\n- **After a successful tap:** the row stays dimmed until the widget re-fetches its data; it doesn't show the new value straight away.\n- **Option values:** the code assumes they are whole numbers, as the brief shows. That should be confirmed with the API job.\n\n**Still needed:** a build and the brief's step 7 checks on a device or emulator. That covers set, change and clear; picking a sport; changes made in the app showing up; the midnight reset; airplane mode; logout; API 24 and 34+; light and dark; and placing it next to the other two widgets.\n\nEverything is committed and the worktree is clean. The summary and the translator's string list are in `docs/jobs/cup_check-in-widget/implementation.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":365,"cache_read_input_tokens":100153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":365},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dae5cf85-b4d2-45c7-b8d0-eb5aafd64190","uuid":"88677e74-55dc-4634-ac02-50749e28384d","timestamp":"2026-10-29T20:57:35.572Z","request_id":"req_011CgXCRHKRckqFxaknvsMFp"}
