{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWtVL8ewsdR3tkaNifGGpn","type":"tool_result","content":"# Implementation: check-in widget\n\nid: cup\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-10-29\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a third home-screen widget, `check-in`. It shows one row per enabled tracker,\neach with up to 6 option buttons tinted with the server's color. Tapping an option\nposts `check_in.set` with an explicit target value. Tapping the selected option\nsends `null`, which clears it. Tapping the tracker name opens the `check_in`\nroute. The midnight reset, 422 handling, row limit and route key were already in\nplace (see tasks.md).\n\nThe prerequisite holds: `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` handles\n`check_in`. Nothing under `frontend/` was edited, and `vendor.sh` was not run.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `WidgetPayload.ROW_ID` now allows `_` (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}`).\n\nTASK-2: `WidgetPayload` parses `scale` actions. New `Option` (value, icon, ARGB\ncolor), and `Item.actionValue` (nullable) and `Item.options`. Options are skipped\nwhen they have an unknown icon (21 known), a color that is not `#RRGGBB`, or a\nvalue that is not an integer. At most 6 are kept. The action is dropped when no\noption is valid. `Item.hasOption(int)` lets the receiver check a tapped value.\n\nTASK-3: `WidgetApi.postAction` has a new overload with an `Integer` value. It sends\n`Content-Type: application/json` and `{\"value\":N}` or `{\"value\":null}`. The\nno-body path is unchanged (fixed length 0, no Content-Type), and status mapping is\nunchanged (422 → `TEMPORARY_FAILURE`).\n\nTASK-4: `WidgetWork.runAction(..., Integer value)` stores `has_value` plus\n`value`; an absent `value` means an explicit null. `WidgetActionWorker` sends a\nbody only when `has_value` is set. Work that older builds enqueued has no flag\nand still posts without a body. Outcome handling is unchanged.\n\nTASK-5: `WidgetActionReceiver` accepts `scale` taps. It reads\n`EXTRA_ACTION_VALUE` and only accepts an `Integer`. It requires the value to be\none of the cached row's options. The target is `null` when the value equals the\nrow's current value, otherwise the value itself.\n\nTASK-6: Added 21 single-color vector drawables, `res/drawable/ic_widget_checkin_*.xml`,\nconverted from lucide-static 1.59.0 (the `@lucide/svelte` version in use). Arc\nflags were normalized for Android's path parser. Custom icons:\n- yoga: from `IconYoga`.\n- water: a cup outline after `IconWater`.\n- food amount: Lucide `pizza`, which `IconPlate` draws.\n- menstruation: the droplet outline of `IconDropletFill`.\n\nTASK-7: New resources:\n- `layout/widget_check_in.xml`: header, list and message.\n- `layout/widget_check_in_row.xml`: tracker name above 6 option slots.\n- `layout/widget_check_in_preview.xml` and `drawable/widget_check_in_preview.xml`.\n- `drawable/widget_check_in_option_selected.xml`, using the new color\n  `widget_selected` in `values` and `values-night`.\n- `xml/check_in_widget_info.xml`: 4×3 target, min 250×180dp, resizable.\n\nTASK-8: Strings in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`. The short error state\nreuses `widget_time_tracking_failed` (\"Couldn't update\"), because the German\n`widget_action_failed` says \"Abhaken fehlgeschlagen\" (checking off failed).\n\nTASK-9: `CheckInWidgetProvider`, modeled on the time tracking provider. It has the\nsame states and \"updated\"/error line, and no section titles. Every row view state\nis set explicitly: icon, tint, highlight, content description, alpha, enabled,\nfill-in and visibility. Unused slots are `GONE`. PendingIntent request codes are 7\nand 8. The kind `CHECK_IN(\"check-in\", …, \"today\")` and the manifest receiver are\nregistered.\n\nTASK-10: **Not run.** This session has no JDK, Android SDK, device or emulator, so\nI could not run `./gradlew assembleDebug` or any of the manual checks. The code is\nunverified by a compiler. A human needs to build the app and do the brief's\nstep 7 checks:\n- set, change and clear mood; pick a sport;\n- app-side check-in and tracker changes show up in the widget;\n- midnight reset;\n- airplane mode (revert and error state);\n- logout;\n- API 24 and 34+; light and dark;\n- next to the other two widgets.\n\n## New strings for the translator\n\n| name | en |\n|---|---|\n| `widget_check_in_name` | Check-in |\n| `widget_check_in_description` | Check in for today from your home screen |\n| `widget_check_in_option` | %1$s: %2$d of %3$d |\n| `widget_check_in_option_selected` | %1$s: %2$d of %3$d, selected |\n\nThe de/fr/es/it versions were written by the developer and need review.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Not compiled and not checked on a device (see TASK-10).\n- Option values are assumed to be integers, as in the brief. Confirm this with the\n  API job.\n- After a successful tap, the row stays dimmed until the re-fetch arrives (the same\n  \"active\" lifecycle as the other kinds). It does not show the new value\n  optimistically.\n- The option content description uses the option's position (\"3 of 5\"), not its raw\n  value.\n- `widget_check_in_option_selected` is a fourth string, beyond the three in the\n  tasks, so screen readers announce which option is selected.\n# Verdict: check-in widget\n\nid: cup\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-10-29\n\n## Review\n\nReviewed `git diff main...HEAD` on `feature/cup_check-in-widget`. Every changed\nfile is covered by a task. Nothing under `frontend/` changed, and no signing,\nversion or F-Droid files changed. All new XML resources are well-formed, and\nthere are 21 option drawables.\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: `WidgetPayload.ROW_ID` is `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}`. The length limit is kept.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `options()` skips options with an unknown icon, a non-`#RRGGBB` color or a\nnon-int value, keeps at most 6, and drops the action when none is left.\n`integer()` rejects doubles and out-of-range longs. A `null` or missing `value`\nbecomes `actionValue = null`. Existing `Item` callers were updated.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: The no-body path is unchanged (fixed length 0, no Content-Type). The body\npath sets `Content-Type: application/json` and a fixed length, and sends\n`{\"value\":N}` or `{\"value\":null}`. Status mapping is shared, so 422 maps to\n`TEMPORARY_FAILURE`.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: A missing `has_value` (old enqueued work) means no body. A present\n`has_value` without `value` sends an explicit null. Outcome handling is unchanged.\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: The value is read as a strict `Integer` and must be one of the cached row's\noptions. The target is `null` when it equals `row.actionValue`, otherwise the\nvalue. Check and button paths are unchanged.\n\nTASK-6: PASS\nnotes: The 21 drawables exist and match the `iconRes` switch, which covers all 21\nof `OPTION_ICONS`. The fill-level icons use the outline shape, as tasks.md\nproposed. Shapes have not been checked visually (no render report exists).\n\nTASK-7: PASS\nnotes: Root, row and preview layouts, the selected-highlight shape, the\n`widget_selected` color for light and dark, and the provider info (4×3,\nresizable, preview, description) are all present.\n\nTASK-8: PASS\nnotes: The strings are in all 5 locales. `widget_check_in_option_selected` is an\naddition beyond the plan, documented in implementation.md and justified for\naccessibility. The translator table is provided.\n\nTASK-9: PASS\nnotes: `CheckInWidgetProvider` follows `TimeTrackingWidgetProvider` for states,\nheader and \"updated\"/error line. Each recycled option view sets icon, tint,\nbackground (0 when not selected), content description, alpha, enabled, fill-in\nand visibility, and unused slots are `GONE`. The title's route fill-in is always\nset (empty when there is no route). Request codes 7 and 8 don't clash with the\nother widgets. The kind and manifest receiver are registered.\n\nTASK-10: FAIL\nnotes: implementation.md says it plainly: no JDK, Android SDK or emulator was\navailable, so `./gradlew assembleDebug` was never run and none of the brief's\nstep 7 checks were done. This review environment has no toolchain either. The\ncode has never been compiled, and the vector paths, RemoteViews reflection calls\n(`setColorFilter`, `setImageAlpha`, `setBackgroundResource`, `setEnabled`) and\nmidnight reset are unverified on a device.\n\n## Security\n\nNot run. One note from this review: fill-in values from the launcher are checked\nagainst the cached options before use (TASK-5), so untrusted extras are never\nsent to the server as-is.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe code review found no defects. One blocker remains before merge:\n\n1. Build the app (`cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug`) and run the brief's\n   step 7 manual checks on a device or emulator (API 24 and 34+, light and dark).\n   Record the results in implementation.md. This needs an environment with a\n   JDK and Android SDK, so a human has to do it if the agent session still has\n   none.\n0582e61 [cup] chore: commit all\nb3d4888 [cup] verdict: code passes, build and device checks pending\n83c4422 [cup] chore: commit all\na70de49 [cup] implementation: add summary\nfda66ea Widget: add the check-in widget\ne1ead9d Widget: add check-in strings\nde84e7c Widget: add check-in layouts and resources\nb932727 Widget: add check-in option icons\n0d87ceb Widget: accept scale taps in the action receiver\n9e63638 Widget: carry action values into the action worker\n5e96530 Widget: post action values as a JSON body\nd289862 Widget: parse scale actions\n8765fc8 Widget: allow _ in row ids\ne9cce56 [cup] chore: commit all\nc02d6af [cup] chore: commit all\n83a5e85 Scaffold job cup_check-in-widget\n2649e1e update frontend\n872bf89 backlog: check-in widget\n2e15204 docs: check-in widget decisions\na562f61 Time tracking widget: move the running timer out of the list so it ticks","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb579395-3e14-4ee4-b7fb-697d8df41cd8","uuid":"66f63617-084a-47f4-bb8a-56b42d6b31df","timestamp":"2026-10-29T2