pe). The body\npath sets `Content-Type: application/json` and a fixed length, and sends\n`{\"value\":N}` or `{\"value\":null}`. Status mapping is shared, so 422 maps to\n`TEMPORARY_FAILURE`.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: A missing `has_value` (old enqueued work) means no body. A present\n`has_value` without `value` sends an explicit null. Outcome handling is unchanged.\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: The value is read as a strict `Integer` and must be one of the cached row's\noptions. The target is `null` when it equals `row.actionValue`, otherwise the\nvalue. Check and button paths are unchanged.\n\nTASK-6: PASS\nnotes: The 21 drawables exist and match the `iconRes` switch, which covers all 21\nof `OPTION_ICONS`. The fill-level icons use the outline shape, as tasks.md\nproposed. Shapes have not been checked visually (no render report exists).\n\nTASK-7: PASS\nnotes: Root, row and preview layouts, the selected-highlight shape, the\n`widget_selected` color for light and dark, and the provider info (4×3,\nresizable, preview, description) are all present.\n\nTASK-8: PASS\nnotes: The strings are in all 5 locales. `widget_check_in_option_selected` is an\naddition beyond the plan, documented in implementation.md and justified for\naccessibility. The translator table is provided.\n\nTASK-9: PASS\nnotes: `CheckInWidgetProvider` follows `TimeTrackingWidgetProvider` for states,\nheader and \"updated\"/error line. Each recycled option view sets icon, tint,\nbackground (0 when not selected), content description, alpha, enabled, fill-in\nand visibility, and unused slots are `GONE`. The title's route fill-in is always\nset (empty when there is no route). Request codes 7 and 8 don't clash with the\nother widgets. The kind and manifest receiver are registered.\n\nTASK-10: FAIL\nnotes: implementation.md says it plainly: no JDK, Android SDK or emulator was\navailable, so `./gradlew assembleDebug` was never run and none of the brief's\nstep 7 checks were done. This review environment has no toolchain either. The\ncode has never been compiled, and the vector paths, RemoteViews reflection calls\n(`setColorFilter`, `setImageAlpha`, `setBackgroundResource`, `setEnabled`) and\nmidnight reset are unverified on a device.\n\n## Security\n\nNot run. One note from this review: fill-in values from the launcher are checked\nagainst the cached options before use (TASK-5), so untrusted extras are never\nsent to the server as-is.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe code review found no defects. One blocker remains before merge:\n\n1. Build the app (`cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug`) and run the brief's\n   step 7 manual checks on a device or emulator (API 24 and 34+, light and dark).\n   Record the results in implementation.md. This needs an environment with a\n   JDK and Android SDK, so a human has to do it if the agent session still has\n   none.\n0582e61 [cup] chore: commit all\nb3d4888 [cup] verdict: code passes, build and device checks pending\n83c4422 [cup] chore: commit all\na70de49 [cup] implementation: add summary\nfda66ea Widget: add the check-in widget\ne1ead9d Widget: add check-in strings\nde84e7c Widget: add check-in layouts and resources\nb932727 Widget: add check-in option icons\n0d87ceb Widget: accept scale taps in the action receiver\n9e63638 Widget: carry action values into the action worker\n5e96530 Widget: post action values as a JSON body\nd289862 Widget: parse scale actions\n8765fc8 Widget: allow _ in row ids\ne9cce56 [cup] chore: commit all\nc02d6af [cup] chore: commit all\n83a5e85 Scaffold job cup_check-in-widget\n2649e1e update frontend\n872bf89 backlog: check-in widget\n2e15204 docs: check-in widget decisions\na562f61 Time tracking widget: move the running timer out of the list so it ticks","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EWtVL8ewsdR3tkaNifGGpn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
