{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\ntotal 1432\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 claude claude    4096 Oct 29 20:58 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 claude claude    4096 Oct 29 20:51 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    6500 Oct 29 20:59 brief.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    5274 Oct 29 20:59 implementation.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude 1414814 Oct 29 20:59 session.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude   10146 Oct 29 20:53 tasks.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    1805 Oct 29 20:59 tokens.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    3636 Oct 29 20:58 verdict.md\n# Brief: check-in widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: cup\nbranch: feature/cup_check-in-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nA third home-screen widget: **today's check-in**. One row per enabled tracker\n(mood, sleep, water, sports, …), each with its tappable values. Tapping a\nvalue saves it for today; tapping the selected value again clears it, as in\nthe app. At local midnight the widget resets to the new day. Tapping a\ntracker's name opens the check-in page.\n\nIt builds on the multi-kind foundation and the action plumbing from the Your\nDay and time tracking widgets. It adds one action type, `scale`. The API and\napp jobs live in other repos; their full contract is in this entry.\n\n**Prerequisite, done by a human before this job starts:** `frontend/` is\nvendored from `solyto/app` with the job \"check-in widget: refresh on changes,\nroute key\". Confirm that `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` handles\n`check_in`; do not run `scripts/vendor.sh`. If it is missing, stop and ask.\n\n## Why\n\nChecking in daily is quicker from the home screen than opening the app.\n\n## Contract with the API and the app\n\n### `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/check-in`\n\nSame headers, envelope and status codes as the other widgets. `data`:\n\n```\n{\n  \"kind\": \"check-in\", \"schema_version\": 1, \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n  \"refresh_at\": \"<ISO 8601 with offset>\",       // next local midnight\n  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },\n  \"sections\": [{ \"key\": \"today\", \"rows\": [{     // one row per enabled tracker, at most 12\n      \"id\": \"<tracker key>\",                      // e.g. \"mood\", \"food_quality\" (contains \"_\")\n      \"title\": \"<translated tracker name>\",\n      \"all_day\": true,\n      \"route\": { \"key\": \"check_in\" },\n      \"action\": {\n        \"type\": \"scale\", \"key\": \"check_in.set\",\n        \"value\": 3,                               // today's value, or null\n        \"options\": [{ \"value\": 1, \"icon\": \"mood_1\", \"color\": \"#EF4444\" }, …]  // 5 or 6\n      }\n  }] }]\n}\n```\n\n- **Option icons:** `mood_1` … `mood_5` (Lucide angry, frown, meh, smile,\n  laugh); `sport_dumbbell`, `sport_bike`, `sport_mountain`,\n  `sport_footprints`, `sport_waves_ladder`, `sport_yoga`; and one icon per\n  other tracker: `sleep`, `dreams`, `food_quality`, `food_amount`, `water`,\n  `work`, `menstruation`, `alcohol`, `smoking`, `social_life`. Use the same\n  icons as the app (`frontend/src/lib/components/check-in/daily/DailyCheckInIcon.svelte`)\n  as vector drawables. An option with an unknown icon is not shown.\n- **Colors** come from the server per option (`#RRGGBB`): tint the icon with\n  it. Native has no color logic of its own.\n- **No section title**: the widget title is enough.\n- The section is left out when no tracker is enabled: show `labels.empty`.\n- New in the format, backwards compatible: action type `scale` with `value`\n  and `options`; Your Day and time tracking ignore it.\n\n### Action: `POST {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/actions/check_in.set/<tracker key>`\n\nSame headers as the other actions **plus** `Content-Type: application/json`\nand a body: `{ \"value\": <option value> }` to set, `{ \"value\": null }` to clear.\nNative decides which: tapping the currently selected value sends `null`,\nany other option sends its value. Always send the explicit target, never a\n\"toggle\", so a retry cannot flip it.\n\n| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | Saved (also when the value was already set) | Re-fetch all placed widgets |\n| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired | Delete the local token, show the signed-out state |\n| 404 | Unknown tracker (or old server) | Re-fetch |\n| 422 | Invalid value (should not happen from widget data) | Revert, short error state |\n| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Revert, \"Please update the app\" |\n| 429 / 5xx / no response | Rate-limited, server or network problem | Revert, short error state |\n\n### Route key\n\n`check_in` (no id): the app opens today's check-in.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Kind:** register `check-in` (path `/api/v1/widgets/check-in`, section\n   key `today`) in the kind registry.\n2. **Row ids:** widen the row id check (`WidgetPayload` `ROW_ID`) to allow\n   `_`, so tracker keys like `food_quality` are valid. Keep the length limit.\n3. **Parser:** read `scale` actions (`value`, `options` with `value`, `icon`,\n   `color`); skip options with unknown icons or invalid colors; drop the\n   action when no valid option is left.\n4. **Actions with a value:** the action fill-in intent carries the tapped\n   option's value; the receiver checks it is one of that row's \n\n... [12467 characters truncated] ...\n\nd option\nsends `null`, which clears it. Tapping the tracker name opens the `check_in`\nroute. The midnight reset, 422 handling, row limit and route key were already in\nplace (see tasks.md).\n\nThe prerequisite holds: `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` handles\n`check_in`. Nothing under `frontend/` was edited, and `vendor.sh` was not run.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `WidgetPayload.ROW_ID` now allows `_` (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}`).\n\nTASK-2: `WidgetPayload` parses `scale` actions. New `Option` (value, icon, ARGB\ncolor), and `Item.actionValue` (nullable) and `Item.options`. Options are skipped\nwhen they have an unknown icon (21 known), a color that is not `#RRGGBB`, or a\nvalue that is not an integer. At most 6 are kept. The action is dropped when no\noption is valid. `Item.hasOption(int)` lets the receiver check a tapped value.\n\nTASK-3: `WidgetApi.postAction` has a new overload with an `Integer` value. It sends\n`Content-Type: application/json` and `{\"value\":N}` or `{\"value\":null}`. The\nno-body path is unchanged (fixed length 0, no Content-Type), and status mapping is\nunchanged (422 → `TEMPORARY_FAILURE`).\n\nTASK-4: `WidgetWork.runAction(..., Integer value)` stores `has_value` plus\n`value`; an absent `value` means an explicit null. `WidgetActionWorker` sends a\nbody only when `has_value` is set. Work that older builds enqueued has no flag\nand still posts without a body. Outcome handling is unchanged.\n\nTASK-5: `WidgetActionReceiver` accepts `scale` taps. It reads\n`EXTRA_ACTION_VALUE` and only accepts an `Integer`. It requires the value to be\none of the cached row's options. The target is `null` when the value equals the\nrow's current value, otherwise the value itself.\n\nTASK-6: Added 21 single-color vector drawables, `res/drawable/ic_widget_checkin_*.xml`,\nconverted from lucide-static 1.59.0 (the `@lucide/svelte` version in use). Arc\nflags were normalized for Android's path parser. Custom icons:\n- yoga: from `IconYoga`.\n- water: a cup outline after `IconWater`.\n- food amount: Lucide `pizza`, which `IconPlate` draws.\n- menstruation: the droplet outline of `IconDropletFill`.\n\nTASK-7: New resources:\n- `layout/widget_check_in.xml`: header, list and message.\n- `layout/widget_check_in_row.xml`: tracker name above 6 option slots.\n- `layout/widget_check_in_preview.xml` and `drawable/widget_check_in_preview.xml`.\n- `drawable/widget_check_in_option_selected.xml`, using the new color\n  `widget_selected` in `values` and `values-night`.\n- `xml/check_in_widget_info.xml`: 4×3 target, min 250×180dp, resizable.\n\nTASK-8: Strings in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`. The short error state\nreuses `widget_time_tracking_failed` (\"Couldn't update\"), because the German\n`widget_action_failed` says \"Abhaken fehlgeschlagen\" (checking off failed).\n\nTASK-9: `CheckInWidgetProvider`, modeled on the time tracking provider. It has the\nsame states and \"updated\"/error line, and no section titles. Every row view state\nis set explicitly: icon, tint, highlight, content description, alpha, enabled,\nfill-in and visibility. Unused slots are `GONE`. PendingIntent request codes are 7\nand 8. The kind `CHECK_IN(\"check-in\", …, \"today\")` and the manifest receiver are\nregistered.\n\nTASK-10: **Handed to the human, as the brief says (\"Ignore testing. Human will test.\").**\nA second developer pass re-read the Java diff for compile-level problems\n(imports, overloads, RemoteViews methods, the 21 drawables against the `iconRes`\nswitch) and found none. It is still not compiled.\n\nOriginal note: **Not run.** This session has no JDK, Android SDK, device or emulator, so\nI could not run `./gradlew assembleDebug` or any of the manual checks. The code is\nunverified by a compiler. A human needs to build the app and do the brief's\nstep 7 checks:\n- set, change and clear mood; pick a sport;\n- app-side check-in and tracker changes show up in the widget;\n- midnight reset;\n- airplane mode (revert and error state);\n- logout;\n- API 24 and 34+; light and dark;\n- next to the other two widgets.\n\n## New strings for the translator\n\n| name | en |\n|---|---|\n| `widget_check_in_name` | Check-in |\n| `widget_check_in_description` | Check in for today from your home screen |\n| `widget_check_in_option` | %1$s: %2$d of %3$d |\n| `widget_check_in_option_selected` | %1$s: %2$d of %3$d, selected |\n\nThe de/fr/es/it versions were written by the developer and need review.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Not compiled and not checked on a device (see TASK-10).\n- Option values are assumed to be integers, as in the brief. Confirm this with the\n  API job.\n- After a successful tap, the row stays dimmed until the re-fetch arrives (the same\n  \"active\" lifecycle as the other kinds). It does not show the new value\n  optimistically.\n- The option content description uses the option's position (\"3 of 5\"), not its raw\n  value.\n- `widget_check_in_option_selected` is a fourth string, beyond the three in the\n  tasks, so screen readers announce which option is selected.\ncat: /workspace/.manigot/manigot.json: No such file or directory","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_013KZSDgkgmUAYQACNgifU9t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae6fad24-abd1-4705-9fa9-4d0c6af071b3","uuid":"3b3a9c9f-ca72-4a8f-b6ab-6a6b8ccc94d4","timestamp":"2026-10-29T20:59:43.122Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\ntotal 1432\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 claude claude    4096 Oct 29 20:58 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 claude claude    4096 Oct 29 20:51 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    6500 Oct 29 20:59 brief.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    5274 Oct 29 20:59 implementation.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude 1414814 Oct 29 20:59 session.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude   10146 Oct 29 20:53 tasks.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    1805 Oct 29 20:59 tokens.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude    3636 Oct 29 20:58 verdict.md\n# Brief: check-in widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: cup\nbranch: feature/cup_check-in-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nA third home-screen widget: **today's check-in**. One row per enabled tracker\n(mood, sleep, water, sports, …), each with its tappable values. Tapping a\nvalue saves it for today; tapping the selected value again clears it, as in\nthe app. At local midnight the widget resets to the new day. Tapping a\ntracker's name opens the check-in page.\n\nIt builds on the multi-kind foundation and the action plumbing from the Your\nDay and time tracking widgets. It adds one action type, `scale`. The API and\napp jobs live in other repos; their full contract is in this entry.\n\n**Prerequisite, done by a human before this job starts:** `frontend/` is\nvendored fro